 no longer see stale prices for up to a day after a price change. This fixes the stale-price support ticket, SUP-881.\n\n## Cause\n\n`PriceCache` stored prices with no timestamp. Entries never expired. A price change reached customers only when the process restarted.\n\n## Change\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `app/cache.py` | `put` stores the price with its fetch time |\n| `app/cache.py` | `get` drops entries older than the TTL and returns `None` |\n| `app/settings.py` | Adds `PRICE_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS`, default 300 |\n\nAn expired entry counts as a cache miss. The caller then fetches a fresh price.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet `PRICE_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS` to change the TTL. A lower value gives fresher prices but more upstream fetches.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\n- This diff adds no tests. Expiry needs one test for a fresh entry and one for an expired entry.\n- Expired entries leave the cache only when someone reads them. SKUs (stock keeping units) that nobody reads again stay in memory.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","ttft_ms":2246,"type":"result","duration_ms":9708,"uuid":"0696fbd1-f051-44a8-a425-7664bb30fd92","ttft_stream_ms":748,"time_to_request_ms":77,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":19,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":1,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":0,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":10,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":8,"request_build":2},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":27,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":141,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"deferred_tools_delta","slowest_producer_ms":9,"cpu_ms":20,"major_faults":0},"first_content_frame_ms":748,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
